# oracle: pair lj/cut/dipole/long 2.5 + kspace_style pppm/dipole 1.0e-4 with the automatic G-ewald and mesh (accuracy 1.0e-4), 108 fcc point dipoles (dipole/random, |mu| 0.7) in a periodic box, run 0: pe, elong, press and the per-atom forces and torques
# oracle-files: w135pd_auto_fcc_tq.dump
# Measured with native LAMMPS (/home/roy/.local/bin/lmp, b332f28): the engine agrees to 1.0e-14 (thermo) and 1.4e-15 (forces and torques). The automatic G-ewald follows the last bits of mu2: adjust_gewald takes one Newton step with a forward-difference derivative (h = 1e-6) of the error estimates, where a one-ulp change of mu2 moves G by 5.6e-6, so mu2 is summed as native does it, per atom (mu_x^2 + mu_y^2 + mu_z^2) in native atom order. Before that the engine summed component by component in its own order: G 1.3859114 against native 1.3859120, ecoul 3.2e-6.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-12 atomrel=1e-12 filerel=1e-11 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      hybrid sphere dipole
boundary        p p p
lattice         fcc 0.4
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
set             group all diameter 1.0
set             group all density 1.0
set             group all dipole/random 4421 0.7
pair_style      lj/cut/dipole/long 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0
kspace_style    pppm/dipole 1.0e-4
# automatic G-ewald and mesh (no kspace_modify)
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl ecoul elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
run             0
write_dump      all custom w135pd_auto_fcc_tq.dump id tqx tqy tqz modify format float %.15g sort id
